  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phytotherapy, Integrative and Complementary Practices to Promote Health</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Centro de Educao Popular (CENEP) promotes the use of medicinal plants indigenous to the Curimata territory in the Brazilian Northeast and works with communities to apply them effectively for health care and conservation. CENEP will expand project activities in the northeastern state of Paraba, to include research on florals made with native plants from this semi-arid region of Brazil, organize the production and sales of healthy foods and expand training programs on complementary health practices. It will benefit approximately 2,350 people directly through the grant activities and another 3,500 rural inhabitants of the Curimata region of Paraba state.</narrative>
  </description>
